5, and on the middle of those grids August to September and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2025, October to November ran 50% of normal on the middle and November to December ran 60%. For 2026 so far, March to April came in at 41% of normal on the middle. The driest year on every grid was 1965, at 61% or 62% of normal.</p>"}
